===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:nyght}}
From {{inh|en|enm|nighte,night,nyght,niȝt,naht}}, from {{inh|en|ang|niht}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*naht|t=night}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*nahts|t=night}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*nókʷts|t=night}}.
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|sco|nicht|t=night}}, {{cog|yol|neeght}}, {{m|yol|nieght}}, {{m|yol|nyeght|t=night}}, {{cog|frr|naacht}}, {{m|frr|Nacht}}, {{m|frr|noach}}, {{m|frr|nåcht|t=night}}, {{cog|stq|Noacht|t=night}}, {{cog|fy|nacht|t=night}}, {{cog|cim,nl|nacht|t=night}}, {{cog|de,nds|Nacht|t=night}}, {{cog|lb|Nuecht|t=night}}, {{cog|mhn|nòcht|t=night}}, {{cog|wym|naocht|t=night}}, {{cog|yi|נאַכט|t=night}}, {{cog|da|nat|t=night}}, {{cog|fo|nátt|t=night}}, {{cog|is|nátt}}, {{m|is|nótt|t=night}}, {{cog|nb,nn,sv|natt|t=night}}, {{cog|gmq-scy|nøtt|t=night}}, {{cog|got|𐌽𐌰𐌷𐍄𐍃|t=night}}; also {{cog|br|noz|t=night}}, {{cog|kw,cy|nos|t=night}}, {{cog|ga|anocht|t=tonight}}, {{cog|gv|noght|t=tonight}}, {{cog|gd|a-nochd}}, {{m|gd|an nochd|t=tonight}}, {{cog|la|nox|t=night}} (whence English {{doublet|en|nox|notext=1}}, a {{glossary|doublet}}), {{cog|el|νύχτα|t=night}}, {{cog|sq|natë|t=night}}, {{cog|ltg,lv|nakts|t=night}}, {{cog|lt|naktis|t=night}}, {{cog|be|ноч|t=night}}, {{cog|bg|нощ|t=night}}, {{cog|cs,pl,sk|noc|t=night}}, {{cog|mk|ноќ|t=night}}, {{cog|ru|ночь|t=night}}, {{cog|sh|ноћ}}, {{m|sh|noć|t=night}}, {{cog|sl|noč|t=night}}, {{cog|uk|ніч|t=night}}, {{cog|xto|nakcu|t=last night; at night}}, {{cog|txb|nekcīye|t=last night; at night}}, {{cog|hit|𒉈𒆪𒊻|tr=nekuz|t=evening, nightfall; dawn, twilight}}, {{cog|sa|नक्त्|tr=nákt}}.
