===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|noen}}, {{m|enm|none}}, {{m|enm|non}}, from {{inh|en|ang|nōn|t=the ninth hour}}, from a Germanic borrowing of classical {{uder|en|la|nōna||ninth hour}} (short for {{m|la|nōna}} {{m|la|hōra}}), feminine of {{m|la|nōnus||ninth}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|noen}}, obsolete German {{m|de|Non}}, Norwegian {{m|no|non}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[time of day]] when the Sun seems to reach its highest point in the sky; [[solar noon]].
#: {{ux|en|On Saturdays, I love to have a lie-in until '''noon'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|The race is due to start at '''noon''' sharp.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1933
|title=w:Twentieth Amendment to the United States Constitution
|text=The terms of the President and Vice President shall end at '''noon''' on the 20th day of January, and the terms of Senators and Representatives at '''noon''' on the 3d day of January, of the years in which such terms would have ended if this article had not been ratified; and the terms of their successors shall then begin.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Chris Boyette|title=Investigators release update on BioLab chemical plant fire probe|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/11/24/us/biolab-fire-georgia-conyers-explosion|date=2024-11-24|passage=The fire was put out by around 8:10 a.m. by the Rockdale County Fire Rescue. But around '''noon''', another fire erupted, according to the CSB.}}
## The [[mean time]] of [[solar noon]], marked as twelve o'clock on most clocks.
# {{lb|en|now|rare}} The corresponding time in the middle of the night; [[midnight]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1789|author=w:Erasmus Darwin|title=The Loves of the Plants|publisher=J. Johnson|page=116
|passage=So the sad mother at the '''noon''' of night / From bloody Memphis stole her silent flight {{...}}.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1885|author=w:Sir Richard Burton|title=The Book of the Thousand Nights and One Night|section=Night 17
|passage=When night was at its '''noon''' I heard a voice chanting the Koran in sweetest accents {{...}}.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} The [[ninth]] hour of the day counted from [[sunrise]]; around three o'clock in the afternoon.
# {{lb|en|figurative}} The highest point; culmination.
#* {{RQ:Motley Dutch Republic|passage=In the very '''noon''' of that brilliant life which was destined to be so soon, and so fatally, overshadowed.}}

