#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2013|month=July-August|author=[http://www.americanscientist.org/authors/detail/catherine-clabby Catherine Clabby]|magazine=w:American Scientist|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/4/focus-on-everything|title=Focus on Everything|passage=Not long ago, it was difficult to produce photographs of tiny creatures with every part in focus. That’s because the lenses that are excellent at magnifying tiny subjects produce a '''narrow''' depth of field. A photo processing technique called focus stacking has changed that.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20130907101436/https://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/4/focus-on-everything}}
# Of little extent; very limited; [[circumscribed]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1675|author=w:John Wilkins|title=Of the Principles and Duties of Natural Religion|passage=The Jews were but a small nation, and confined to a '''narrow''' compass in the world.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} {{U|restrictive}}; without [[flexibility]] or [[latitude]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''narrow''' interpretation}}
# Contracted; of limited scope; [[bigoted]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''narrow''' mind}}
#: {{ux|en|'''narrow''' views}}
# Having a small [[margin]] or degree.
#: {{ux|en|a '''narrow''' escape}}
#: {{ux|en|The Republicans won by a '''narrow''' majority.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1970|author=Reading Reform Foundation|title=The Annual Reading Reform Foundation Conference|page=47|passage=Although we lost the election by the '''narrowest''' of margins, the people of Oregon heard a great deal about education, and particularly about how "look-say" reading instruction was hardshipping Oregon school children.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=March 29, 2007|author=Michael Wines|title=Zimbabwean Leaders Accused of Abducting Opponents|work=w:The New York Times|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2007/03/29/world/africa/29zimbabwe.html
|passage={{...|Given those power struggles, one Harare political analyst said Wednesday,}} it is unclear whether the beatings of potential political opponents are a governmentwide strategy or a '''narrower''' effort by Mr. Mugabe’s backers to shore up his remaining power.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20200622231206/https://www.nytimes.com/2007/03/29/world/africa/29zimbabwe.html}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=September 18, 2011|author=Ben Dirs
|title=Rugby World Cup 2011: England 41-10 Georgia|work=w:BBC Sport
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/rugby_union/14959055.stm
|passage=As in their '''narrow''' defeat of Argentina last week, England were indisciplined at the breakdown, and if Georgian fly-half Merab Kvirikashvili had remembered his kicking boots, Johnson's side might have been behind at half-time.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20211127172533/https://www.bbc.com/sport/rugby-union/14959055}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} Limited as to means; [[straitened]]
#: {{ux|en|'''narrow''' circumstances}}
