|text=Isoamyl acetate (''banana''): This familiar scent is known to most noses as the primary odor '''note''' in bananas and pears.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[observation|Observation]]; [[notice]]; [[heed]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Merchant of Venice|V|i|passage=Go in ''Nerriſſa,'' / Giue order to my ſeruants, that they take / No '''note''' at all of our being abſent hence, / Nor you ''Lorenzo, Ieſſica'' nor you.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1625|author=w:Francis Bacon|chapter=Of ceremonies and reſpects|title=The Works of Francis Bacon|volume=III|location=London|publisher=J. and J. Knapton et al.|year_published=1730|page=373|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=VHNUAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA373|passage=So it is true, that ſmall matters win great commendation, becauſe they are continually in uſe, and in '''note''' ; whereas the occaſion of any great virtue cometh but on feſtivals.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[reputation|Reputation]]; [[distinction]].
#: {{ux|en|a poet of '''note'''}}
