|passage={{...}} the seventh century is the '''nadir''' of the human mind in Europe {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1950|author=Elizabeth Janeway|editor=Helen Hull|title=The Writer’s Book
|passage=In this '''nadir''' of poetic repute, when the only verse that most people read from one year’s end to the next is what appears on greetings cards, it is well for us to stop and consider our poets.}}
