===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} A [[contractile]] form of [[tissue]] which [[animal]]s use to effect movement.
#: {{syn|en|thew}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Muscle''' consists largely of actin and myosin filaments.}}
#* {{RQ:Grew Cosmologia Sacra|chapter=Of the Use of Organized Bodies|para=18|page=27|passage=For as the Trunk of the Body, is kept from tilting forvvard by the '''Muſcules''' of the Back: So, from falling backvvard, by theſe of the Belly.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} An [[organ]] composed of muscle tissue.
#* {{RQ:Grey Riders of the Purple Sage|chapter=VIII|passage=His brow and hair and the palms of his hands were wet, and there was a kind of nervous contraction of his '''muscles'''. They seemed to ripple and string tense.}}
#* {{RQ:Orwell Animal Farm|chapter=I|passage=You, Boxer, the very day that those great '''muscles''' of yours lose their power, Jones will sell you to the knacker {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|usually|in the plural}} A well-developed [[physique]], in which the muscles are [[enlarged]] from [[exercise]].
#* '''2008''', Lou Schuler, "Foreward", ''in'' Nate Green, ''Built for Show'', page xii
#*: The fact that I was middle-aged, bald, married, and raising girls instead of chasing them didn't really bother me. '''Muscles''' are cool at any age.
# {{lb|en|uncountable|figurative}} [[strength|Strength]], [[force]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=14 Feb 88|volume=15|number=30|journal=Gay Community News|page=1|title=Arizona Impeaches Right-Wing Governor|author=Elizabeth Pincus|text=The widely-backed campaign to recall Evan Mecham as governor of Arizona gained even more '''muscle''' when the state House of Representatives voted to impeach the ultraconservative on February 5.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2010|author=Adam Quinn|title=US Foreign Policy in Context|page=81|passage=The lesson to be drawn from the events of 1914, to Roosevelt's mind, was that civilization needed '''muscle''' to defend it, not just solemn words.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=John D. MacDonald|title=The Long Lavender Look|page=15|passage=It was going to take '''muscle''' to pluck Miss Agnes out of the canal.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 January 12|author=Christian Wolmar|title=A new year... but the same old mistakes are being made|journal=RAIL|issue=948|pages=40–41|passage=How can the unions - or more specifically the RMT—possibly think this is a good time to exert a bit of industrial '''muscle''' and indulge in strikes both on the national railway and the London Underground?}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|figurative}} Hired [[strongman|strongmen]] or [[bodyguard]]s.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1985|author=w:Lance Parkin|title=The Infinity Doctors|page=34|passage=It was easy enough to dodge him, let him crash into the floorboards. Peltroc knew that his priority was the leader, not the hired '''muscle'''.}}

