====Usage notes====
Using a bare noun for an adverb {{cln|hu|conversions}} is typical for times of the day like {{m|hu|reggel||morning}}, {{m|hu|este||evening}} etc., but not for time units like ''minute, hour, week, month,'' or ''year'', which all take a suffix when used as adverbs ({{m|hu|[[percben]], [[órában]], [[héten]], [[hónapban]], [[évben]]}}). Even {{m|hu||nap}} takes {{m|hu||-on}} in most cases other than those above. However, the bare form also occurs in compound adverbs such as {{m|hu|aznap}}, {{m|hu|másnap}}, {{m|hu|mindennap}} and {{m|hu|vasárnap}} (the latter functions as a noun too), as well as {{m|hu|tegnap}} and {{m|hu|holnap}}.

