#: {{syn|en|nerve up|Thesaurus:strengthen}}
#: {{ux|en|The liquor '''nerved up''' several of the men after their icy march.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1907|year_published=1980|author=w:Barbara Baynton|title=Human Toll|series=Portable Australian Authors: Barbara Baynton|editors=Sally Krimmer; Alan Lawson|publisher=University of Queensland Press|location=St Lucia|page=289|passage=The shock '''nerved''' her, and she ran aimlessly till she fell, and for a time lay, but making a barrier of her arms, that the child should not be crushed.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} To [[perform]] a [[neurectomy]] on (someone or something).
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=8 January 1993|author=Penny E. Breyer|title=Net wisdom needed on '''nerving'''|newsgroup=rec.equestrian|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250821131900/https://groups.google.com/g/rec.equestrian/c/O7jrzLqNaqE/m/V5YwRVDG_DQJ|passage=She has been trying everything (wedge pads, bar shoes, etc.) and he is still dead lame. Someone has suggested '''nerving''' him, which (I believe - correct me if I am wrong!) involves cutting the main nerve in his foot so he can be ridden without pain.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=18 June 1999|author=CJ|title=Advice for horse that keeps mouth open & runs through the bit?|newsgroup=rec.equestrian|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250821131213/https://groups.google.com/g/rec.equestrian/c/9DeWMyS5FjA/m/XpnyWkAEaQAJ|passage=You can't '''nerve''' a hoof and I didn't realize that the cannon bone where the nerving takes place is not part of the leg.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=24 March 2002|author=lpgirl|title='''nerving''' tails|newsgroup=rec.equestrian|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250821132126/https://groups.google.com/g/rec.equestrian/c/YpmLfq2eog0/m/mvR3ft8ohl8J|passage=Her instructor was trying to convince me that her horse's tail "needed" to be '''nerved'''.}}
#* {{see more citations|en}}
# {{senseid|en|get on someone's nerves}} {{lb|en|transitive|informal|rare}} To [[get on someone's nerves|get on (someone’s) nerves]]; to [[annoy]], [[irritate]], or [[bother]] (someone).
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=1 July 1996|author=Tuennes|title=FDDI or Ethernet or what?|newsgroup=comp.dcom.lans.ethernet|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250821125752/https://groups.google.com/g/comp.dcom.lans.ethernet/c/938WOx1SDO0/m/2mmmLTYzAGkJ|passage=I guess, my previous message never came in the net..so again: (hope, i don't '''nerve''' anyone) We want to combine different LAN's via fiberoptic cable (Monomode) to the Internet.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2024|author=Michael Kobzan|chapter=Return to The Berserker|chapterurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=M_QqEQAAQBAJ&pg=PT112|title=John Dunley|isbn=9798224419661|passage=No way was I assured, but after that the doctor refused to answer anymore questions. Instead, he wouldn’t stop '''nerving''' me to give him a guided tour of the berserker.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2025|author=Simone Janson|chapter=Better Choice - 10 Tips: Properly informing instead of brooding!|chapterurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=L-gTEAAAQBAJ&pg=PT24|title=Yes, No, Maybe? What to Do When You Don’t Know What You Want|publisher=Best of HR|isbn=9783965963276|passage=Do not '''nerve''' others: Of course it helps to talk to others. But just when you've got a lot of information, that can be annoying.}}
#* {{see more citations|en}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|informal|rare}} To be [[nervous]].
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=8 May 1997|author=Mathias Schiffer|title=!Damiac14's Page Updated, and improved!|newsgroup=comp.lang.basic.visual.misc|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250821132925/https://groups.google.com/g/comp.lang.basic.visual.misc/c/CLO6g7SoxnE/m/AUqEU9EgKoQJ|passage=Mathias slowly leads his hand down to the holster... yeah, cool steel... his fingers wrap around the grip of his Smith & Wesson's, dragging it out, aiming and... In other words: Stop '''nerving''', damiac14!}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=24 December 1998|author=TUTonNO|title=REM Thieves?- a hint|newsgroup=alt.my.head.hurts|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250821131724/https://groups.google.com/g/alt.my.head.hurts/c/ijByDPzVWB0/m/h2CSur4x5UwJ|passage=use the extrapolar solution, don't '''nerve'''.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=22 March 2006|author=JimKG@aol.com|title=Most dangerous place you have gone with a camera?|newsgroup=misc.transport.road|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250821132800/https://groups.google.com/g/misc.transport.road/c/PQ7PSZW7cqk/m/8MHWvnnvsZcJ|passage=Speaking of Camden, I pulled off I-676 once to clean my windshield on the side of some surface street before turning around to shoot the Ben Franklin Bridge Westbound and I must say I was a bit nervous knowing the reputation, and I don't "'''nerve'''" easily.}}
