# {{lb|en|geometry}} The [[point]] at which a [[curve]] [[cross]]es itself, being a [[double point]] of the curve. See {{m|en|crunode}} and {{m|en|acnode}}.
# {{lb|en|geometry}} A similar point on a [[surface]], where there is more than one tangent-plane.
# {{senseid|en|graph}} {{lb|en|graph theory}} A [[vertex]] or a [[leaf]] in a [[graph]] of a [[network]], or other element in a [[data structure]].
# {{lb|en|medicine}} A hard [[concretion]] or [[incrustation]] which forms upon bones attacked with [[rheumatism]], [[gout]], or [[syphilis]]; sometimes also, a swelling in the neighborhood of a joint.
# {{lb|en|physics}} A point along a [[standing wave]] where the wave has minimal [[amplitude]].
# {{lb|en|rare}} The knot, [[intrigue]], or [[plot]] of a dramatic work.
# {{lb|en|technical}} A hole in the [[gnomon]] of a [[sundial]], through which passes the ray of light which marks the hour of the day, the [[parallel]]s of the Sun's [[declination]], its place in the [[ecliptic]], etc.
# {{senseid|en|word of interest}} {{lb|en|computational linguistics}} The [[word]] of interest in a [[KWIC]], surrounded by left and right [[cotext]]s.
# {{lb|en|electronics}} A region of an [[electric]] [[circuit]] connected only by (ideal) [[wire]]s (i.e. the [[voltage]] between any two points on the same node must be zero).
# {{lb|en|syntax}} A point in a [[parse tree]] that can be assigned a [[syntactic]] [[category]] label.
# {{lb|en|biology}} A point in a [[cladogram]] from which two clades branch, representing the presumed ancestor.

